# D1 GIVEN the conventions open-items, tasks/todo.md chips and unchecked boxes,
#    repository launch/submission/shipping markers, and current live backend
#    state, WHEN the audit is complete, THEN every actionable item is reconciled
#    in LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md and stale completed items are explicitly closed.
# D2 GIVEN each checklist row, WHEN independently reviewed, THEN it names exactly
#    one owner (Adam or machine), an evidence-backed status, and an exact command,
#    repository path, or Firebase/Xcode/App Store Connect console path to close it.
# D3 GIVEN the Spec 08 expected members, WHEN checked against local and live
#    evidence, THEN Twilio/SMS, five affiliate URLs, source:resolved review, Test
#    Mover replacement, kit supplier, Xcode StoreKit pass-through, privacy/auth
#    legal work, and App Store asset/metadata refresh all appear without assuming
#    they are complete.
# D4 GIVEN the completed Spec 08 implementation, WHEN docs are synchronized, THEN
#    CLAUDE.md, peezy-conventions-v2.md, peezy-v1-architecture.md, and
#    peezy-v1-catalog-sheet.md record the 47-row catalog, verify layer,
#    accountability and kit-calibration contracts, and LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md as the
#    single source of launch work.
# D5 GIVEN the Phase D diff, WHEN documentation checks, the exact iPhone 17 Pro
#    build, a fresh-context validator, and diff review run, THEN D1-D4 receive
#    evidence-backed PASS/FAIL before a separate Phase D commit; no function,
#    rules, catalog, vendor, provider, ISP, or workflow deployment occurs.
